ed version. So, I should mention that the timeline is included but also offer to trim any unnecessary details if that's what they want. I want to make sure it aligns with their expectations while keeping it informative!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Done.\n\n**What changed**\n- Added a normalized `user_summary` object to the depression pipeline script.\n- It now maps raw tracking fields into display-ready labels:\n  - **Voice Depression Detection** → `Class`, `Confidence`, `Inference time`\n  - **Fuzzy Stress Evaluator** → `Stress level`, `Score`, `Lambda`, `Confidence`, `Explanation`, `Timeline`\n- Updated the skill instructions to prefer `user_summary` when available.\n\n**Verified**\n- I re-ran the script successfully and confirmed it now returns `user_summary`.\n\nExample shape now returned:\n```json\n\"user_summary\": {\n  \"Voice Depression Detection\": {\n    \"Class\": \"Moderate\",\n    \"Confidence\": 11.3\n  },\n  \"Fuzzy Stress Evaluator\": {\n    \"Stress level\": \"Moderate\",\n    \"Score\": \"0.385\",\n    \"Lambda\": 0.3851116997420148,\n    \"Timeline\": [...]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**What it means**\n- Future callers can read one clean block instead of remapping raw fields each time.\n\n**Next sensible step**\n- If you want, I can do one final cleanup: make `Timeline` excluded from `user_summary` by default unless a `--include-timeline` flag is passed, so the default output stays compact.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_00f817b97194c8740169dd15cc75408191ad8957dafeea21a5\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":65061,"output":309,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":65370,"cost":{"input":0.1626525,"output":0.004635,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.1672875}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776096712113}}
